(Personalized Psychological Intervention for Fibromyalgia: Randomized Protocol for) Tj
T*
(Assessing Cognitive-Behavioral Therapy as an Adjunct to Routine Care) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Fibromyalgia syndrome represents a common chronic pain disorder with associated) Tj
T*
(psychological comorbidities including anxiety, depression, and sleep disruption.) Tj
T*
(Cognitive-behavioral interventions show promise in fibromyalgia management, yet evidence) Tj
T*
(for individualized programs delivered alongside standard medical care remains limited.) Tj
T*
(This protocol describes a single-blinded randomized trial enrolling 70 participants) Tj
T*
(meeting diagnostic criteria at a tertiary rehabilitation center. The intervention arm will) Tj
T*
(receive 10 weeks of therapist-administered individualized cognitive-behavioral programming) Tj
T*
(tailored to each participant's specific symptom profile and psychosocial stressors,) Tj
T*
(delivered concurrently with ongoing routine pharmacologic and rehabilitative treatment.) Tj
T*
(Control participants continue standard care alone. Outcome domains encompass validated) Tj
T*
(measures of anxiety, depression, sleep architecture, emotional processing, and disease-) Tj
T*
(specific functional capacity. This study will clarify whether personalized psychological) Tj
T*
(intervention augments treatment response in this population.) Tj
